  "dateReleased": "2026-06-10",
  "releaseNotes": "B1.0 to B1.2 Beta update: refines LIFX Light Manager from the initial beta into a cleaner local-LAN management build. Adds first-click Discovery reliability, corrected discovery/device-count reporting, improved device preparation table layout, inline discovered-light local naming, optional child-device name prefixing, and clearer child creation/update behaviour. Adds optional lightweight LAN-only switch-state polling using LIGHT.GET_POWER, now enabled after child-device creation at a safe 2-minute default interval. Retains the Master Switch aggregate device and the local child drivers for Mono, Tunable White, Colour and Colour+IR capable lights. Firmware discovery remains excluded from the normal discovery path to keep scans fast and reduce unnecessary LAN chatter. No LIFX Cloud polling is used for runtime status updates.",
